# Meta AI Config

## Golden rule
**Source of truth:** `docs/ai-bootstrap/` → `setup.sh` → `.cursor/` + `.claude/`
Never edit `.cursor/` or `.claude/` directly.

## When this rule applies
- Editing bootstrap templates, workflow docs, `CLAUDE.md`, or `AGENTS.md`
- User asks to add/update rules, skills, or hooks
- New stack, convention, or recurring pattern needs AI guidance

## Required skill
Follow `.cursor/skills/meta/maintain-ai-config/SKILL.md` (or `.claude/skills/...`).

## Quick decision
| Need | Artifact |
|------|----------|
| Always-on constraint | Rule (`global` or dept) |
| Multi-step how-to | Skill |
| Deterministic enforcement | Hook |
| Deep reference | `docs/workflows/*.md` |

## After every change
```bash
./docs/ai-bootstrap/setup.sh
./docs/ai-bootstrap/validate-ai-config.sh
```
Update `SKILLS_INDEX.md` + `SKILLS_CHANGELOG.md`.

## Parity
Cursor `cursor/` and Claude `claude/` subtrees must stay mirrored.
